# Testing Guide — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

**Coverage now:** run `{{COVERAGE_CMD}}`. **Gate:** {{COVERAGE_GATE}}, enforced in CI.

## Principles

1. **Fast.** Unit tests run in milliseconds; the whole unit suite in under a minute.
2. **Isolated.** No shared state, no order dependence, no network in unit tests.
3. **Clear.** The test name states the intent; a failure points at the cause.
4. **Stable.** Flaky tests are fixed or quarantined with `@wip` the same day, never retried into green.
5. **Honest.** A stale test is updated to the new requirement. It is never weakened or skipped to pass.

## Test types

| Type | Location | Runs | Needs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Unit | `{{UNIT_DIR}}` | `{{UNIT_CMD}}` | nothing external (mock upstreams) |
| Integration | `{{INTEGRATION_DIR}}` | `{{INTEGRATION_CMD}}` | local services only |
| End-to-end | `{{E2E_DIR}}` | `{{E2E_CMD}}` | a running app (`BASE_URL`), fixtures or credentials |

Unit tests follow Arrange → Act → Assert, one behavior per test, and mock at the boundary
(HTTP client, repository), not in the middle of the code under test.

## E2E tag taxonomy

Tags decide where a scenario runs. Every scenario carries exactly one *kind* tag and any
number of *domain* tags.

| Tag | Kind | Meaning | CI | Nightly |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `@smoke` | kind | app shell loads, key elements render | yes | yes |
| `@api-only` | kind | hits the backend HTTP API, no browser | yes | yes |
| `@live-api` | kind | needs real upstream credentials | **no** | fixture mode only |
| `@wip` | kind | being written or quarantined | **no** | **no** |
| `@<domain>` | domain | one per feature area ({{DOMAIN_TAGS}}) | per kind | per kind |

- **CI** runs `not @live-api and not @wip` in fixture mode.
- **Full e2e** (the IssueFlow gate) runs `not @wip` in fixture mode against a fresh server.
- **Live validation** runs `@live-api` scenarios with real credentials, by hand or nightly.

## API modes: fixture, live, record

The app reads `{{API_MODE_VAR}}` and the e2e suite runs the same scenarios in all three modes.

| Mode | Value | What happens | When |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Fixture | `fixture` (default) | upstream calls are replayed from `{{FIXTURES_DIR}}` | CI, local dev without credentials |
| Live | `live` | real upstream calls | regression validation, new features |
| Record | `record` | live, and every upstream response is saved as a fixture | after an upstream contract changes |

Re-record with the IssueFlow tool, then commit the fixtures so fixture mode keeps working
without credentials:

```bash
bash $SKILLS_HOME/IssueFlow/Tools/e2e.sh --record <worktree>
git add {{FIXTURES_DIR}} && git commit -m "chore(e2e): re-record fixtures"
```

Fixtures must never contain secrets. Scrub tokens and personal data in the recorder.

## Running e2e locally

```bash
# full suite on a fresh server, torn down afterwards (the gate IssueFlow runs)
bash $SKILLS_HOME/IssueFlow/Tools/e2e.sh <worktree>

# a subset, against a server you started yourself
BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:{{PORT_BASE_BACKEND}} {{E2E_CMD}} -- --tags "@smoke"
```

Visual debugging knobs ({{E2E_DEBUG_KNOBS}}) are documented in `{{E2E_DIR}}/README.md`.

## Coverage targets

| Area | Target | Priority |
| --- | --- | --- |
| {{CRITICAL_AREA}} | 90%+ | critical |
| Integrations / adapters | 80%+ | high |
| API endpoints | 85%+ | high |
| Utilities | 75%+ | medium |
| Startup / configuration | 60%+ | low |

The CI gate is the floor ({{COVERAGE_GATE}}). Raise it when the suite earns it; never lower it
to pass.

## What CI does with tests

Lint → security → unit (runtime matrix) → coverage gate → e2e in fixture mode with placeholder
secrets → summary. The nightly workflow runs the full non-`@wip` suite and keeps screenshots and
reports as artifacts. The same lint/type commands are the local `PREFLIGHT_CHECKS`, so a green
preflight means a green lint job.
